#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096336 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6624681a-bb00-59db-8df9-4d5a3cd00434" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3627" :question/problem "Given that $y=5\\ln x$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d} x}\\left(\\ln x \\right)= \\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} & = \\left(5\\ln x\\right)' \\\\ & = 5 (\\ln x)' \\\\ &=5\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x} \\\\ &= \\dfrac{5}{x}. \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096337 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/id #uuid "58d47fb0-cf75-58c4-8eea-f3ae97333159" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3628" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=2\\ln x+x^2-1$, find $f'(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f'(x) &= \\left(2\\ln x+x^2-1\\right)' \\\\ &=2 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x}+2x-0 \\\\ &=\\dfrac{2}{x}+2x. \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096338 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/id #uuid "f61ac550-d62c-558f-b6d5-0d4c9aba8089" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3629" :question/problem "Given that $y=4\\log_3 x$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "Here, we apply our formula for the derivative when the base of the logarithm is a number other than $e$. By doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}&=\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4\\log_3 x\\right) \\\\ &=4\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\log_3 x\\right) \\\\ &=4\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{x \\ln 3} \\\\ &=\\dfrac{4}{x \\ln 3}. \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096339 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "5eaa00f8-0fd0-5de6-a7c0-965db6de3a5c" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3630" :question/problem "Given that $y= \\log_4 x + \\ln x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=1$." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nat that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} &= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\log_4 x + \\ln x \\right) \\\\ &= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\log_4 x) + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\ &= \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 4} + \\dfrac{1}{x}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x = 1} &= \\left.(\\frac{1}{x\\ln 4} + \\frac{1}{x})\\right|_{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\ln 4} + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0a9fbee-97de-5587-b7a8-2d739e0fe564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245474} {:answer/id #uuid "a7947555-2e57-5f4f-bf99-afa3f6a77b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{ex}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245475} {:answer/id #uuid "12c43f05-d3c8-5787-88bc-d74b2140e83e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{e}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245476} {:answer/id #uuid "f2917bd1-e152-5c82-86ba-e2ae1b7192e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245477} {:answer/id #uuid "75c5f459-5594-5cd4-a272-5968b3072748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0a9fbee-97de-5587-b7a8-2d739e0fe564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245474} :answer-field/id #uuid "15bb7789-c52a-5826-a94d-628ed429ea81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245473}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21ad6958-9427-54e1-9344-a853dd625138" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-101600" :question/problem "Given that $y=2eln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2eln⁡x) \\\\  & =2e\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =2e\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "829656d8-9eda-533c-a503-e7e692a2e836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245481} {:answer/id #uuid "02155d95-9ced-5d74-9ac2-ed709daea0d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245482} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2c25e6-fb95-5502-9bd6-0f31a1ca3865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245483} {:answer/id #uuid "7b6a62b2-2601-5caa-920c-d957ca190c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245484} {:answer/id #uuid "a156b127-a1ef-59f9-aabb-bba6463fc4ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "829656d8-9eda-533c-a503-e7e692a2e836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245481} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4df4eb7-3c15-5c5b-9c08-e489fbd6a2a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245480}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41046d62-8496-5dc8-8432-1ac2a083b39f" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-101604" :question/problem "Given that $y=-9ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-9ln⁡x) \\\\  & =-9\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =-9\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cce0c84-c685-50fc-9b8a-2aa09beceb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8ln⁡2-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245488} {:answer/id #uuid "e123e87a-e4a8-5478-b894-ca12a0c3b993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245489} {:answer/id #uuid "0087b9e7-d990-5afe-bf25-05b0f5e679b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245490} {:answer/id #uuid "61faf0e6-9753-5efc-8e83-5626a7286113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245491} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b69e23-1708-5452-93d0-c61120caf67c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+8ln⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e123e87a-e4a8-5478-b894-ca12a0c3b993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245489} :answer-field/id #uuid "2775a343-375d-52d8-917d-1077e70e9cd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245487}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6722baff-8f94-5523-b159-d7215bb8efed" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-101726" :question/problem "Given that $y=3x-5+8{log}_{2}⁡x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-5+8{log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-5)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5)+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =3-0+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{8}{xln⁡2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1/ln⁡2} & ={(3+\\frac{8}{xln⁡2})|}_{x=1/ln⁡2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{8}{(\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}\\cdot ln⁡2)} \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa3e3522-489e-59f6-8e5f-95c329a1e83b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{ln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245495} {:answer/id #uuid "5591f0c1-38a4-5729-9d53-05affdff490d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245496} {:answer/id #uuid "edaf6a2d-3375-5cce-a3ac-72e6f7c69528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245497} {:answer/id #uuid "c33ca7f9-c577-55c4-a628-64c57b7a9928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245498} {:answer/id #uuid "0d9cdf29-eaea-5e04-b7ac-f2912934ab3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edaf6a2d-3375-5cce-a3ac-72e6f7c69528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245497} :answer-field/id #uuid "434e9897-1fb5-55a8-b1a1-9c83067e3386" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245494}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1a79eda-9c98-57d8-82ba-6cc467cf56bf" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-105256" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={7}^{x}+{log}_{5}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({7}^{x}+{log}_{5}⁡x) \\\\  & ={7}^{x}\\cdot ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5} \\\\  & ={7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bca459d4-24ee-5244-be09-0b354d2fd41c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245502} {:answer/id #uuid "55e5e9b5-791b-58f5-b06e-737d5a6a3df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245503} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5b6fc0-ad37-5d7f-b9b9-3838ddb541fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245504} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6545d1-acb3-5aa5-bb63-3d8fdf40e9f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245505} {:answer/id #uuid "1e274a1b-978c-5239-94b6-10ea3ac41edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{xln⁡4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55e5e9b5-791b-58f5-b06e-737d5a6a3df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245503} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4109101-faa5-5fcf-815e-725f3f2df85b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245501}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67b94213-d99a-5858-9eec-4b43c51db6fc" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-11900" :question/problem "Given that $y=5{log}_{4}⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d753fb-803f-544d-bd2b-ae27118df148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245509} {:answer/id #uuid "61ebb04e-f644-5583-b219-9dfd47b4c9f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245510} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cba0cd-8957-5e8d-8e0d-d61138fed645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245511} {:answer/id #uuid "5a352986-a14d-596b-b068-507c3ce813f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245512} {:answer/id #uuid "245189c2-ee04-53f2-a75c-8c1448cff1b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a352986-a14d-596b-b068-507c3ce813f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245512} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1ab46a2-1aa3-5797-a068-c2b994d24788" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245508}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90eeb8c1-b715-5c75-b93c-b100adff5ce0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-11911" :question/problem "Given that $y=2x+ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+ln⁡x) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6f1fc24-e635-5984-9781-b963abcb7872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245516} {:answer/id #uuid "46c1c6b5-499e-54ff-9b95-cc180e94c084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245517} {:answer/id #uuid "3c6a07e7-7a9c-5129-b97e-d5b4f1ea1eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245518} {:answer/id #uuid "ac3917b5-e932-59d2-a842-22250ea88b3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245519} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f15fc5-3ca2-56b4-b1c8-93b3a58550e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c6a07e7-7a9c-5129-b97e-d5b4f1ea1eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245518} :answer-field/id #uuid "728ea165-ea1e-56e8-bbd6-61a719febc59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245515}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f651874-7846-5bc8-b0e8-ba6c0958a8ef" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-17371" :question/problem "Given that $y=3ln⁡x+2{x}^{2}-5x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3ln⁡x+2{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3ln⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+4x-5 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{x}+4x-5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{3}{x}+4x-5)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1}+4\\cdot 1-5 \\\\  & =3+4-5 \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "431948e7-17ca-5c28-9a19-a45757fde1b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245523} {:answer/id #uuid "068442a1-36ec-5a46-9b5a-9d85cce2c3f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245524} {:answer/id #uuid "6090286d-84c6-5880-8d77-3e783b52596e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245525} {:answer/id #uuid "00781f68-ca87-5150-b9ad-f98485704bfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245526} {:answer/id #uuid "e6aae0ab-e147-565a-9c7b-d259a7949a5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "068442a1-36ec-5a46-9b5a-9d85cce2c3f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245524} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcbb4dbb-ff3f-552a-b17b-0469fb9832ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245522}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "104d7814-9b21-55a2-864d-c61ec56f5c8f" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-17392" :question/problem "Given that $y=2{x}^{e}-ln⁡x$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{e}-ln⁡x) \\\\  & =2e{x}^{e-1}-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(2e{x}^{e-1}-\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =2e\\cdot {1}^{e-1}-\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =2e-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0007031-6988-5651-8ffd-23a0653ca80b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11^{x}\\ln x - \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094845} {:answer/id #uuid "e078d70c-63de-5091-a233-58995f88f619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 11 + \\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094846} {:answer/id #uuid "0e65bf25-ab30-5820-986d-a4e0abba72f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11^{x}\\ln 11 - \\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094847} {:answer/id #uuid "3906a9fd-f9f0-55ef-9a8b-8a52ddaac104" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11^{x} - \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094848} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd68bb6-f2a7-5e79-82dc-a81ebf4a5b5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11^{x} - \\ln 11 - \\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e65bf25-ab30-5820-986d-a4e0abba72f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11^{x}\\ln 11 - \\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094847} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae9af3c-c67b-5547-98d7-93de5f6971b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094844}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1cb4423b-343c-5035-85a6-f38acaa8835d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-1919" :question/problem "Find $f^{′}(x)$ for $f(x) = 11^{x} - 5\\ln x$." :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({11}^{x}-5ln⁡x) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}\\cdot ln⁡11-5(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}ln⁡11-\\frac{5}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e90703a-fe9a-5005-bf53-7738b5423a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e90703a-fe9a-5005-bf53-7738b5423a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245530} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f9609a1-8b91-52eb-8d91-c281b09f6dcf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245529}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "754b7256-bb68-5676-b86f-e67821b5f20a" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-308849" :question/problem "Given that $y=8ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8ln⁡x) \\\\  & =8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e07748e0-3b33-5acf-bd17-ae66fa3e5a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07748e0-3b33-5acf-bd17-ae66fa3e5a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245533} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec0062d0-fc51-5cc3-996f-d593aace7f83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245532}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3d54b3eb-ded4-5c5a-8cec-34fe12561ac5" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-308854" :question/problem "Given the function  $y=3{x}^{e}+ln⁡x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{e}+ln⁡x) \\\\  & =3e{x}^{e-1}+\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(3e{x}^{e-1}+\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =3e\\cdot {1}^{e-1}+\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =3e+1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245534 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d84e113-0113-5137-9533-627f1404eb23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245536} {:answer/id #uuid "3e9cded4-f07c-5cbd-a713-216728655018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e9cded4-f07c-5cbd-a713-216728655018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245537} :answer-field/id #uuid "87f26ece-1d63-520e-80d4-b015ed89ec4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245535}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2e26e30-590f-58b8-b40b-aad2e7b0b3b6" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-339949" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\frac{11}{4}ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{11}{4}ln⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2ad5a6f-3194-5f3a-9982-fd2336c2ddec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2ad5a6f-3194-5f3a-9982-fd2336c2ddec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245540} :answer-field/id #uuid "6388562b-2b4c-50ea-b269-9fc34ebf91c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245539}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7d4e29bb-15ef-5e11-8db1-eae3045391ca" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-339950" :question/problem "Given that $y=-\\frac{7}{3}ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{7}{3}ln⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28ba94f1-8641-5046-815b-84bde6bb5f82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55+\\frac{1}{\\ln(6)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245543} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e2ea69-8c24-540e-922a-84258e3995fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55-\\frac{1}{\\ln(6)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9e2ea69-8c24-540e-922a-84258e3995fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55-\\frac{1}{\\ln(6)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245544} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e517cf4-1992-5a23-8a87-f2a675cf83b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245542}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce4d4f97-d868-5d04-a9b5-17c6975fb577" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-339994" :question/problem "Given the function $y=2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+1-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡6} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =6(3)^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{3\\cdot ln⁡6} \\\\  & =55-\\frac{1}{ln⁡6}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c185dc-f80c-572e-971e-402d1e522644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24-\\frac{5}{2\\ln(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c185dc-f80c-572e-971e-402d1e522644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24-\\frac{5}{2\\ln(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245547} :answer-field/id #uuid "874e7ee2-08f7-52fa-b075-9d0504a30ed5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245546}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13209240-47ee-57bb-950d-c7141b5c2f2d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-340024" :question/problem "Given the function $y=2{x}^{3}-5{log}_{3}⁡x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-5{log}_{3}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{3}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡3} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{xln⁡3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(6{x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{xln⁡3})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =6(2)^{2}-\\frac{5}{2ln⁡3} \\\\  & =24-\\frac{5}{2ln⁡3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca43d93f-962c-5867-9383-d3b927df358c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\frac{6}{\\ln(2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245550} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5d6dfc-5e0b-5f82-a0f8-d66383f2bfe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+\\frac{6}{\\ln(2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c5d6dfc-5e0b-5f82-a0f8-d66383f2bfe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+\\frac{6}{\\ln(2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245551} :answer-field/id #uuid "29cb8dbd-f48c-52ed-9849-93f8f108d09f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245549}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2bb23fc-94e4-5068-ad8c-2bac28d89d6c" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-340026" :question/problem "Given the function $y=6{log}_{2}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-3x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=1$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{log}_{2}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-3x) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x)+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡2}+4\\cdot 2x-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{xln⁡2}+8x-3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{6}{xln⁡2}+8x-3)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1\\cdot ln⁡2}+8(1)-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{ln⁡2}+5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2ecb11f-9df4-5980-805e-ecff46f0849a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{4}{3}\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2ecb11f-9df4-5980-805e-ecff46f0849a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{4}{3}\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245554} :answer-field/id #uuid "28bf96d3-4622-5427-88e4-78f942b675bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245553}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2c81546-e71f-5118-8492-272c58b3d5ed" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-340104" :question/problem "Given the function  $y=4ln⁡x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}+5$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=2$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4ln⁡x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}+5) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}ln⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}ln⁡(2))|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{2}ln⁡(2) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{4}{3}ln⁡(2)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0478ae9-d95a-52af-be9e-d907429eb223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3^x\\ln(3)+\\frac{1}{x\\ln(10)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0478ae9-d95a-52af-be9e-d907429eb223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3^x\\ln(3)+\\frac{1}{x\\ln(10)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245557} :answer-field/id #uuid "61329a65-511b-5206-bac7-c7f9c1558f79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245556}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00bcd86f-d2c5-50f7-a8a4-315cf0884886" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-340105" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}+log⁡x$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}+log⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(log⁡x) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}ln⁡(3)+\\frac{1}{xln⁡(10)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "001c73a9-6be2-5573-b9af-d22000144c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^x+\\frac{3}{x\\ln(5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "001c73a9-6be2-5573-b9af-d22000144c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^x+\\frac{3}{x\\ln(5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245560} :answer-field/id #uuid "c095fa52-1272-5aee-8f54-e8ebbaf05a6b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245559}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2848146e-3aa0-5434-8c1e-21d5642b4d56" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-340106" :question/problem "Given that $y=-{e}^{x}+3{log}_{5}⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{x}+3{log}_{5}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{5}⁡x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡(5)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}+\\frac{3}{xln⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db2996e5-0f5c-57b9-a673-8be6139f81d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^3+\\frac{1}{\\ln(2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245563} {:answer/id #uuid "96dd115d-eb77-539d-8e19-9ce168522313" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^3-\\frac{1}{\\ln(2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96dd115d-eb77-539d-8e19-9ce168522313" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^3-\\frac{1}{\\ln(2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245564} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ab0476c-ced0-566f-b65d-c2395fa7b54b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245562}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa34e2cc-02df-5659-bdbd-d89b4f453804" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-340110" :question/problem "Given the function $y=4{e}^{x}-3{log}_{2}⁡x+7,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=3$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}-3{log}_{2}⁡x+7) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7) \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡2}+0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{xln⁡2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{xln⁡2})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{3}{3\\cdot ln⁡2} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
